            "answer": {
              "short": "See the divided bar chart. Segment lengths are proportional to the faculty counts.",
              "worked": "Use an overall bar length of 10 cm. For each faculty, segment length is its student count divided by 2250, multiplied by 10 cm.\n$$\\begin{align*}L_{\\text{Science}}&=\\frac{225}{2250}\\times10=1\\text{ cm}\\\\L_{\\text{Medicine}}&=\\frac{125}{2250}\\times10=\\frac59\\text{ cm}\\\\L_{\\text{Law}}&=\\frac{54}{2250}\\times10=0.24\\text{ cm}\\\\L_{\\text{Arts}}&=\\frac{815}{2250}\\times10=\\frac{163}{45}\\text{ cm}\\\\L_{\\text{Commerce}}&=\\frac{620}{2250}\\times10=\\frac{124}{45}\\text{ cm}\\\\L_{\\text{Engineering}}&=\\frac{411}{2250}\\times10=\\frac{137}{75}\\text{ cm}\\end{align*}$$\nLabel the six segments. Percentages shown on the chart are rounded to one decimal place where necessary.",
