            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "See the pie chart. Sector angles, in table order: $36^\\circ$, $20^\\circ$, $8.64^\\circ$, $130.4^\\circ$, $99.2^\\circ$, $65.76^\\circ$.",
              "worked": "Calculate each sector angle as its fraction of the total multiplied by $360^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\theta_{\\text{Science}}&=\\frac{225}{2250}\\times360^\\circ=36^\\circ\\\\\\theta_{\\text{Medicine}}&=\\frac{125}{2250}\\times360^\\circ=20^\\circ\\\\\\theta_{\\text{Law}}&=\\frac{54}{2250}\\times360^\\circ=8.64^\\circ\\\\\\theta_{\\text{Arts}}&=\\frac{815}{2250}\\times360^\\circ=130.4^\\circ\\\\\\theta_{\\text{Commerce}}&=\\frac{620}{2250}\\times360^\\circ=99.2^\\circ\\\\\\theta_{\\text{Engineering}}&=\\frac{411}{2250}\\times360^\\circ=65.76^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nThe angles total $360^\\circ$. Draw the sectors using a protractor and label each faculty.",
              "solutionDiagrams": [
                {
                  "id": "p31-q4-pie-solution",
